{"model": "Chatterbox Turbo (MLX 8-bit)", "segments": [{"text": "Unlike Ruby on Rails, Android app development does not have as definitive of an opinion on how apps should be developed and so we have designed our own pattern leveraging open source tools like Otto and Retrofit to design our applications.", "block": 0, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/1dd273a777ead1388952a8740def8e5b5c8b31add5c15f26a322c4446fef6f5e.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.38], [1, 0.38, 0.66], [2, 0.66, 0.88], [3, 0.88, 1.1], [4, 1.76, 2.0], [5, 2.0, 2.26], [6, 2.26, 2.72], [7, 2.72, 2.94], [8, 2.94, 3.1], [9, 3.1, 3.28], [10, 3.28, 3.46], [11, 3.46, 3.86], [12, 3.86, 4.1], [13, 4.1, 4.2], [14, 4.2, 4.54], [15, 4.54, 4.72], [16, 4.72, 4.92], [17, 4.92, 5.28], [18, 5.28, 5.48], [19, 5.48, 5.62], [20, 5.62, 6.06], [21, 6.36, 6.42], [22, 6.42, 6.62], [23, 6.62, 6.94], [24, 6.94, 7.08], [25, 7.08, 7.4], [26, 7.4, 7.64], [27, 7.64, 7.86], [28, 7.86, 8.2], [29, 8.2, 8.66], [30, 8.66, 8.98], [31, 8.98, 9.22], [32, 9.22, 9.58], [33, 9.58, 9.88], [35, 10.18, 10.34], [36, 10.34, 10.82], [37, 10.82, 11.08], [38, 11.08, 11.34], [39, 11.34, 11.54], [40, 11.54, 12.06]]}, {"text": "After much research, we at Spark Start invested in developing a design pattern for our client applications that leverages the best practices.", "block": 1, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/e964bc47031c3212584b062c33f981d90997c392fc76e37645a65df658bd4f81.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.3], [1, 0.3, 0.46], [2, 0.46, 0.98], [3, 1.18, 1.24], [4, 1.24, 1.36], [7, 1.8, 2.2], [8, 2.2, 2.52], [9, 2.52, 2.9], [10, 2.9, 3.06], [11, 3.06, 3.3], [12, 3.3, 3.64], [13, 3.64, 3.88], [15, 3.98, 4.14], [16, 4.14, 4.78], [17, 4.78, 5.16], [18, 5.16, 5.6], [19, 5.6, 5.78], [20, 5.78, 6.08], [21, 6.08, 6.56]]}, {"text": "Jumping right in here:", "block": 1, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/6e76927e800b4543b4dfbd4cd4dacc4bcead67696e8e845425c22921d1f9a610.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.44], [1, 0.44, 0.6], [2, 0.6, 0.82], [3, 0.82, 1.1]]}, {"text": "##Consuming a RESTful API", "block": 2, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/f45bdef7f717be0c63f711561fcb975112c36931f19488e2b31e41af329a0215.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.52], [1, 0.52, 0.7], [2, 0.7, 1.18], [3, 1.18, 1.6]]}, {"text": "Following Object Oriented Programming’s best practices, all objects should each only have one job.", "block": 3, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/07a345a57bda897ab30735f3d9f943807ea5e0a9abc55777b755d67b70727bc3.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.44], [1, 0.44, 0.96], [2, 0.96, 1.44], [3, 1.44, 2.26], [4, 2.26, 2.46], [5, 2.46, 2.96], [6, 3.52, 3.64], [7, 3.64, 3.94], [8, 3.94, 4.22], [9, 4.22, 4.44], [10, 4.44, 4.74], [11, 4.74, 4.92], [12, 4.92, 5.24], [13, 5.24, 5.58]]}, {"text": "With the start of a new api, create a folder with the name of the API you are trying to consume.", "block": 3, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/91532eb701b9926aec79d78754a19e4263d1be39ffe254492b0f1ab1af82bd2a.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.18], [1, 0.18, 0.32], [2, 0.32, 0.54], [3, 0.54, 0.78], [4, 0.78, 0.9], [5, 0.9, 1.14], [6, 1.14, 1.68], [7, 2.2, 2.3], [8, 2.3, 2.44], [9, 2.44, 2.74], [10, 2.74, 2.96], [11, 2.96, 3.08], [12, 3.08, 3.26], [13, 3.26, 3.44], [14, 3.44, 3.58], [15, 3.58, 3.98], [16, 3.98, 4.22], [17, 4.22, 4.3], [18, 4.3, 4.6], [19, 4.6, 4.78], [20, 4.78, 5.12]]}, {"text": "Inside of your client.java file, you will include your retrofit interface classes.", "block": 4, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/7a06eea63c47ed80baefacf07826d610758d18d3967d881df4f08d2b19c83424.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.36], [1, 0.36, 0.56], [2, 0.56, 0.64], [4, 1.48, 1.88], [5, 2.18, 2.28], [6, 2.28, 2.38], [7, 2.38, 2.72], [8, 2.72, 2.94], [9, 2.94, 3.46], [10, 3.46, 4.04], [11, 4.04, 4.62]]}, {"text": "This file will specify how your app will be calling the API.", "block": 4, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/668182a407f80571c971a754c97ca3121cd95b890a515f873fd35ad92bd7649b.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.22], [1, 0.22, 0.46], [2, 0.46, 0.66], [3, 0.66, 1.0], [4, 1.0, 1.32], [5, 1.32, 1.48], [6, 1.48, 1.68], [7, 1.68, 1.82], [8, 1.82, 1.92], [9, 1.92, 2.22], [10, 2.22, 2.4], [11, 2.4, 2.78]]}, {"text": "```java APIClient.java public class APIClient { interface IUser { @GET(“/users/Me.json”) void getMe(Callback callback);", "block": 5, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/b17ad98f15c5af904a455589fc4f2ca150d71adbdb107b2386a4996cf26d5815.mp3"}, {"text": "This keeps all of our API information in one small maintainable file.", "block": 6, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/5548263238289f3199da221b8b7b44785aa2d7991be370a41048b4698b6047e5.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.2], [1, 0.2, 0.44], [2, 0.44, 0.7], [3, 0.7, 0.82], [4, 0.82, 0.94], [5, 0.94, 1.28], [6, 1.28, 1.92], [7, 1.92, 2.12], [8, 2.12, 2.32], [9, 2.32, 2.68], [10, 2.8, 3.26], [11, 3.26, 3.58]]}, {"text": "Notice how we are always using the retrofit callback method instead of the async call.", "block": 6, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/26f96dc93a8e14cb0c641c4ca833d9ea54ebdfb57679f067e9689727a7b1e752.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.28], [1, 0.28, 0.52], [2, 0.52, 0.76], [3, 0.76, 0.86], [4, 0.86, 1.16], [5, 1.16, 1.56], [6, 1.56, 1.76], [7, 1.76, 2.3], [8, 2.3, 2.78], [9, 2.78, 3.14], [10, 3.14, 3.48], [11, 3.48, 3.68], [12, 3.68, 3.8], [13, 3.8, 4.14], [14, 4.14, 4.36]]}, {"text": "This will allow our code to start a web request on any thread.", "block": 6, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/e3cc4ef9868d5a7183126fd1ed47048670dc32a47eedb96e3c3dad5e5369c0d1.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.22], [1, 0.22, 0.36], [2, 0.36, 0.6], [3, 0.6, 0.76], [4, 0.76, 1.0], [5, 1.0, 1.18], [6, 1.18, 1.34], [7, 1.34, 1.44], [8, 1.44, 1.58], [9, 1.58, 1.9], [10, 1.9, 2.14], [11, 2.14, 2.36], [12, 2.36, 2.66]]}, {"text": "Now the code consuming this will never have to worry about thread locking.", "block": 6, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/ff49f0ef9e6de5aa178a36df2c659546f4c566abb2d912fa0855ef19d89e0baf.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.24], [1, 0.24, 0.36], [2, 0.36, 0.58], [3, 0.58, 1.02], [4, 1.02, 1.32], [5, 1.32, 1.48], [6, 1.48, 1.78], [7, 1.78, 2.0], [8, 2.0, 2.16], [9, 2.16, 2.36], [10, 2.36, 2.56], [11, 2.56, 2.84], [12, 2.84, 3.22]]}, {"text": "```java APIManager.java public class APIManager { private Bus mBus;", "block": 7, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/ecea3aa117ef704ad99e65a769c02e169c9a7e258ddf50b039189c3db4e3cb38.mp3"}, {"text": "When the login fragment is resumed, otto automatically subscribes the fragment to the bus.", "block": 8, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/4727b0deb852f378f27cb014ca49f59ce6625818922bc5e55e74b1523aa8b36a.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.16], [1, 0.16, 0.26], [2, 0.26, 0.54], [3, 0.54, 0.88], [4, 0.88, 1.1], [5, 1.1, 1.62], [7, 2.14, 2.64], [8, 2.64, 3.32], [9, 3.32, 3.44], [10, 3.44, 3.74], [11, 3.74, 3.94], [12, 3.94, 4.04], [13, 4.04, 4.18]]}, {"text": "When it is paused, it unsubscribes.", "block": 8, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/984eaf3d1b5398b96d868021ec74f6e5c78fd25515b9765fcf06c71a3d5096ce.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.24], [1, 0.24, 0.34], [2, 0.34, 0.46], [3, 0.46, 1.06], [4, 1.46, 1.56]]}, {"text": "This is awesome, because if a request is initiated to the API, but then the fragment is closed before the rest api responds, we don’t have the fragment still listening for that response.", "block": 8, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/8f3023b56d914f93465c0cfbb61c9e658debcf229ef7b24b4f91a4c3d4f116a3.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.2], [1, 0.2, 0.32], [2, 0.32, 0.56], [3, 0.56, 0.9], [4, 0.9, 1.24], [5, 1.24, 1.26], [6, 1.26, 1.52], [7, 1.52, 1.8], [8, 1.8, 2.26], [9, 2.26, 2.48], [10, 2.48, 2.6], [11, 2.6, 2.98], [12, 3.58, 3.72], [13, 3.72, 3.88], [14, 3.88, 3.96], [15, 3.96, 4.24], [16, 4.24, 4.4], [17, 4.4, 4.74], [18, 4.74, 5.24], [19, 5.24, 5.42], [20, 5.42, 5.6], [21, 5.6, 5.96], [22, 5.96, 6.44], [23, 6.98, 7.12], [24, 7.12, 7.26], [25, 7.26, 7.42], [26, 7.42, 7.56], [27, 7.56, 7.88], [28, 7.88, 8.18], [29, 8.18, 8.52], [30, 8.52, 8.76], [31, 8.76, 8.9], [32, 8.9, 9.26]]}, {"text": "##Conclusion", "block": 9, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/772b4e82c7bddba20aaee6ca73f0539cfe8e2317451de5322a7861b07556b2a0.mp3"}, {"text": "Otto and retrofit play really nicely together and are great tools for building an android app.", "block": 10, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/eafb40ac0516c0b2ea101ceb0bf1cbbdd00065882209f6d9531169b7ac712f61.mp3", "words": [[1, 0.3, 0.52], [2, 0.52, 0.96], [3, 0.96, 1.18], [4, 1.18, 1.44], [5, 1.44, 1.7], [6, 1.7, 2.2], [7, 2.2, 2.44], [8, 2.44, 2.54], [9, 2.54, 2.82], [10, 2.82, 3.2], [11, 3.2, 3.46], [12, 3.46, 3.7], [13, 3.7, 3.94], [15, 4.3, 4.52]]}, {"text": "Managing all of the events can get a bit ugly, so be careful how you name them and organize them in the project.", "block": 10, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/683702a3cfdff75d8d14fa8cc08f77f24375e6227cc3b6223562741b6dd43db7.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.52], [1, 0.52, 0.78], [2, 0.78, 0.92], [3, 0.92, 1.04], [4, 1.04, 1.4], [5, 1.4, 1.72], [6, 1.72, 1.9], [7, 1.9, 1.98], [8, 1.98, 2.1], [9, 2.1, 2.44], [10, 2.72, 2.9], [11, 2.9, 3.02], [12, 3.02, 3.34], [13, 3.34, 3.58], [14, 3.58, 3.72], [15, 3.72, 3.92], [16, 3.92, 4.12], [17, 4.12, 4.3], [18, 4.3, 4.66], [19, 4.66, 4.96], [20, 4.96, 5.08], [21, 5.08, 5.18], [22, 5.18, 5.58]]}]}